body:
Agentic authoring (library form): `kalide init-library <path>` writes an `AGENTS.md` at the library root — a single Markdown file giving coding agents a complete, accurate reference for authoring a kalide template library. The guide is written ONLY when no `AGENTS.md` already exists at the library root: a pre-existing `AGENTS.md` never blocks init-library and is left byte-for-byte untouched (the library is still created normally). It is the library/template-author counterpart of the deck guide (agent-authoring): it documents the same format but leads with library authoring so an agent can create and extend templates. It covers: the `templates/` layout (`library.yaml`, `slides/<name>/`, `sections/<name>/`, `themes/<name>/`, `media/` — templates-dir-layout, library-guide-layout); `library.yaml` (name identifier `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*`, optional `description`, required `format: 1`); the `template.yaml` schema and the `example.md` convention (template-manifest, field-types, body-rules, template-composition, template-variants, number-date-formats); the Go html/template layout language with the v1 `media` helper and the reserved `.deck`/`.slide` context (template-language, template-context, deck-data-in-templates); themes (token-only, no built-in theme) and media reference rules (theme-selection, template-media); and how to validate the library by pointing a deck at it and running `kalide start`, or listing it with `kalide templates`. It states that a library with no templates is load-valid but a library intended to host a deck must provide the deck's theme (external-template-library, theme-selection). Like the deck guide, it is written verbatim from a static file embedded in internal/scaffold, is unbranded (no EY branding and no reference to files under `brand/`), text-only and offline, is not a template asset, and is inert to loading: it is never parsed, validated, rendered, listed or served (global.constraint.no-embedded-template-assets, requirements.constraint.brand-not-embedded). The library layout ignores non-library root entries, so this guide is permitted (library-guide-layout).

AC:
- immediately after `kalide init-library ../lib`, `../lib/AGENTS.md` exists and `../lib` still loads cleanly (templates-dir-validation);
- a deck pointed at `../lib` still validates and serves (the guide is inert);
- the guide contains no EY branding and no reference to files under `brand/`;
- the guide documents every field type, the `media` helper, the reserved context keys and the `template.yaml` keys, so an agent can author a new template without reading Go source;
- scaffolding into a library directory that already holds an `AGENTS.md` succeeds and leaves that file byte-for-byte unchanged; the scaffolded `AGENTS.md` is written only when none exists.
